# Syncly — Development Environment Variables Example
#
# Syncly is a zero-build, privacy-first Manifest V3 Chrome Extension.
# User data and settings are stored locally in chrome.storage.local.
# No environment variables are required for standard runtime execution.

# Optional: Path to custom Google Chrome binary for running Puppeteer smoke tests
# CHROME_PATH="C:/Program Files/Google/Chrome/Application/chrome.exe"
